  "version": 1,
  "name": "Example accounts",
  "_comment": [
    "A preset is a bag of accounts. Every key under \"fields\" matches a data-f",
    "attribute in index.html; anything you leave out falls back to the markup",
    "default, and anything unrecognised is ignored, so it is safe to start from",
    "a partial file. \"slug\" names the exported PNGs, \"label\" is what the",
    "dropdown shows.",
    "Values are inserted as HTML, so <br> and <b> work — which also means you",
    "should only open preset files you trust.",
    "Copy this file, edit it, and load it with the Load… button. To have it",
    "picked up automatically, add the filename to presets/index.json."
  ],
